## Problem

When fork choice stops moving the head (the stuck-head bug in #24620), the node still reports itself synced. Validators keep getting duties, attestation data and block production on a head that cannot become canonical, so they attest to and build on a stale chain.

## Changes

The served head lags (`headLag` in `sync_tolerance.go`) when:
- there is no head state, as before (`not synced`);
- it does not descend from the justified block that `get_head` starts from: it is below that block's slot, or its ancestor at that slot is another block. This covers a head older than the checkpoint and a head left on a branch fork choice moved away from. A justified block or a path that the fork graph does not hold (after a checkpoint sync or a prune) counts as descending. A resolved answer is remembered per served head and justified checkpoint, since the parent links between them do not change, so `/eth/v1/node/health`, `/eth/v1/node/syncing` and gated requests do not walk the ancestry each time;
- a block more than one epoch past it was imported on top of it (`HasImportedDescendantAfter`).

The last two answer `served head is behind fork choice`, so a stuck head is told apart from initial sync.

`HasImportedDescendantAfter` walks the child index from the head:
- It first keeps only the head's children on a reachable variant (below) that no invalidation cut off. With none left it returns at once, so an excluded branch costs about 200 ns whatever its size.
- It counts only blocks that pass `get_head`'s justification and finalization check, judged like `getFilterBlockTree` but only under those children, and without children an invalidation cut off: a block whose remaining children are all cut off is judged as a leaf, as `get_head` judges its EMPTY node.
- It skips blocks that an invalidation cut off: an invalid pre-Gloas block and its children, or a Gloas child of an invalid parent payload.
- At the selected head, it counts only children on the payload variant `get_head` could walk to. A child on the other variant counts only while that variant is not a candidate (an unavailable FULL). The selected head node is published lock-free from `publishSelectedHead`. A changed payload decision clears it, since it can rule out the published variant; until `get_head` publishes again, children of both variants count. When Gloas `get_head` finds no viable node and falls back to the justified root on EMPTY, the head is published as PENDING, so both variants count as well.

Only descendants of the head count, so a chain-wide gap, a lighter fork or a block that was seen but not imported does not trip it.

Effects:
- `/eth/v1/node/health` and `/eth/v1/node/syncing` report syncing.
- Block production, attestation data, PTC data and attester/proposer/sync/PTC duties answer 503. Block production checks its parameters first, so a malformed request still gets 400.
- Pool attestation submissions are not gated. They are validated and published as before, since a valid attestation may come from another node's data.

## Tests

- `forkchoice_test.go`:
  - descendants only;
  - invalidation cut-off, including the pre-Gloas boundary;
  - a branch outside the filtered block tree does not count, the same branch with a viable justification does;
  - a block viable only through a descendant on its invalidated payload does not count; it does as a viable EMPTY leaf, or when the payload is not invalidated;
  - the fallback head of a Gloas `get_head` without viable nodes counts both variants: a viable grandchild below an unavailable FULL payload is seen;
  - the served variant (five cases);
  - after a payload decision changes, children of both variants count;
  - `GetHead` publishes the selected node;
  - with the real head selection: the stuck-head case, a child on the FULL variant of a parent without a payload status, is seen; a healthy EMPTY or FULL head shows no lag.
- `sync_gate_test.go`:
  - the tolerance boundary;
  - descent from the justified block, including the unknown cases, a justified block before its epoch start, a head below the justified block whose path was pruned, and the remembered answer;
  - the two error messages;
  - health and syncing;
  - block production and every gated endpoint through the mux;
  - pool submissions and `builder_boost_factor` on a lagging head.

  These tests fail cleanly (no crash) when the gate is removed.
- `epbs_test.go`: `getSelectedHead` without a head state.
- `node_health_test.go`: main's synced-health test gets a state head for the gate.

Each behaviour change was red first or mutation-checked.

`go test -race` passes for `cl/beacon/...`, `cl/phase1/forkchoice/...` and `cl/phase1/stages`; `make lint` is clean twice.

`BenchmarkHasImportedDescendantAfter` (`head_lag_bench_test.go`), a chain on the FULL variant below the served head, 16-core dev machine: excluded (served EMPTY, payload available) 0.19 to 0.21 µs and 288 B at 128 and 7,200 descendants, against 11.2 µs and 702 µs before the first-step filtering; counted (served FULL) 17 µs and 1.3 ms, unchanged and linear in the subtree.

